# 01 — Prime work cycle
version: 001
Authorization: draft — 2026-10-30
who: Codex Prime
state: Director-agreed first integration scope; no runtime adoption
Face: 01
PPPP: 0415
book: 00.00.10.work

## Goal

Make a small useful Prime cycle over one explicitly registered work book:
read the work evidence, supply judgment, record it with the work, then read the
updated state without manually maintaining a second status account. Current Prime
uses the accepted build before a cold-Prime contextual Colab. Actual model testing
and a change of Prime are separate actions; this design launches neither.

## Responsibility

Director supplies direction, consequential decisions and resources. Prime supplies
interpretation, attributed reasons, review disposition and one bounded next action.
Compute gathers exact evidence, checks supported bindings/holds, records submitted
judgment and derives the view. A label is not identity authentication; a tool's
success does not grant authority. No new provider, role, scheduler or router.

## Read

One proposed read operation takes an explicit desk/book registration and reports
named work, source basis, changed/new/unreviewed returns, recorded holds, completed
passes, completed goals, missing/conflicting records and recorded next actions.
Use exact return custody, page observations and existing view/brief helpers. Prime
chooses the next action. Read never invents priority or a current assignment.
It produces a source-bound decision template with mechanical fields already filled
and a revision/fingerprint suitable for rejecting a stale later submission.

The read path must support explicitly declared real work-book sources read-only.
A historical Git blob, current working file and live custody observation keep their
own provenance. Missing data and legacy unstructured reviews stay visible. Do not
silently interpret an old Accepted sentence as a new typed completion declaration.
Registration owns scope and paths, not an independently editable status ledger.

## Record

One proposed record operation takes Prime's completed decision template, explicit
scope, exact source/return/receipt identities and expected prior state. It validates
and writes the attributed review beside the work through a declared review output
location. Keep the structured record and its readable projection together and bound.
It then derives the desk view from those work-local records. Do not require Prime
to separately update coordination arrays, a global acceptance list and 00.live.

Refuse or retain an explicit incomplete state on changed sources, wrong origin,
stale prior state, conflicting review identity or interrupted writes. Identical
replay is a no-op; a later different decision needs explicit new identity and
lineage. Preserve original returns, prior reviews, exact Director replies and
local reasons. No silent overwrite, hidden retry or inferred approval.

The canonical review records are work-local. Indices and readable desk views are
rebuildable projections. A cache is not an independent source of truth. Define
which completion marker makes a write usable; partial output must never be read as
accepted/complete work. Record failures and provide a bounded inspect/recovery
procedure. Do not claim an unimplemented transaction across multiple stores.

## Completion

Keep separately: review disposition, pass completion and work-page goal completion.
Prime must explicitly declare each relevant terminal state and its evidence under
the existing grant. An accepted correction can finish its pass and leave the page
goal open. A held decision cannot silently become completed. An old page-complete
decision cannot cover a new scope or changed goal without an explicit source-bound
successor. Missing terminal declarations stay unknown/open, not presumed complete.
Existing projection batch semantics must not be relabelled as whole-page closure.

## First delivery and use

0515.prime-cycle builds the adapter in a new lab and exercises the cycle on a small
disposable book. Reuse reviewed tools; document each call, any unsupported mapping
and what remains supplied by Prime. No global integration rewrite. Give current
Prime an exact guide and read-only preview for registered real work, without
Builder mutation of live pages or premature canonical 00.live migration.

After review, Prime performs a real bounded read-record-read. Only after that do
we prepare a contextual N7NN Colab for a fresh test Prime with a disposable book,
clear purpose and permissions, no hidden answer key, and no desk authority transfer.
Record correctness, interventions, confusion, operations/time when exposed and
unknown usage honestly. Synthetic tests do not establish model performance.
